<title>USA: 50-Off says rights offering successful.</title>
<headline>50-Off says rights offering successful.</headline>
<dateline>SAN ANTONIO 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>50-OFF Stores Inc, which is operating in Chapter 11 bankruptcy, said it had received subscriptions for the required minimum with respect to its rights offering.</p>
<p>The offering is to stockholders of record on March 21, 1997 of not less than 30,500 units at $100.00 per unit.</p>
<p>Each unit is comprised of 20 shares each of the new Series A preferred stock and the new common stock the company proposes to issue and sell upon its reorganization plan being confirmed by a bankruptcy judge.</p>
<p>A confirmation hearing has been set for June 3.</p>
<p>50-Off Stores said it will continue to manage its affairs and operate its business under Chapter 11 as a debtor in possession while the plan is being considered.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
